Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:41:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] X0 determinism census

First EXEC phase: the static determinism census that every later
execution phase inherits.

- crates/aura-exec: hand-written WASM binary classifier (magic,
  version, section framing/order, imports, tables, memories, globals,
  every instruction of every function body) with a fail-closed
  opcode whitelist and no engine linked.
- CENSUS: 16 published nondeterminism sources with policy and
  enforcement layer; Ban (18 variants), Verdict, CensusReport,
  ModuleLimits::restrictive() (512 KiB module, 4096 pages, 1024
  table entries), a single float_ban() choke point.
- 21 independent vectors (5 allowed / 16 banned) assembled by
  tools/gen_x0_vectors.py; 4 tests in aura-exec/tests/x0_census.rs.
- 6 negative controls -> 110 total; zero new crates (95 external).
- Evidence: docs/evidence/x0/ (gates, report, inventory, nc.log,
  SHA256SUMS) + x0-dependency-addendum.txt.
- D9 truth pass: STATUS/README stop calling aura-exec a placeholder,
  the measured block and the 'what is missing' list match the tree.

Measured: 184 Rust tests, 4415 vectors in 18 fixtures, 110 NC,
15 crates (10 implemented, 5 placeholders), 0 validators / 0 blocks /
0 transactions.
